<item><title>BHH Maudsley Refurbishment</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The objective of this project is to extend the operational life and improve the utilisation of the existing Maudsley Building at the Baillie Henderson Hospital through refurbishment and adaptive reuse, transforming the former mental health ward into a contemporary administrative workplace for Darling Downs Health.<br /><br />The project will serve as a pilot implementation of Adaptable Administrative Workspace Design Principles, providing an opportunity to evaluate activity-based working environments and inform future workplace planning initiatives across Darling Downs Health.<br /><br />The refurbishment will address identified building deficiencies, including ventilation, moisture management, compliance and amenity issues, while maximising the value of the existing asset and supporting increasing administrative accommodation demands associated with the transition to a single-campus model at Baillie Henderson Hospital and the planned opening of the New Toowoomba Hospital.<br /><br />Recognising that the Maud...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Darling Downs Hospital and Health Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 02/Sep/2026 04:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519696<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 11]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=8d549e2766654417a30f14606c3dd4aas519696</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">8d549e2766654417a30f14606c3dd4aa</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 06:58:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Architecture, Design, Planning</category>
<category>Building Trade, Repairs, Maint.</category>
