<item><title>Customer Rail Transfer Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Queensland Rail invites suitably qualified and accredited passenger transport operators to submit proposals for the provision of Customer Rail Transfer Services. The opportunity includes passenger transfer services across three regional service areas:<br /><br />•	Maryborough West – Hervey Bay RailBus Service<br /><br />•	Proserpine – Airlie Beach/Shute Harbour RailBus Service<br /><br />•	Bowen Transfer Service<br /><br />These services play a key role in connecting customers to Queensland Rail Travel's long-distance rail network and supporting tourism and regional communities throughout Queensland. Queensland Rail is seeking experienced operators that can demonstrate strong safety performance, compliance systems, operational capability and a commitment to delivering high-quality customer service. <br /><br />This opportunity is being managed through Queensland Rail's SAP Ariba Sourcing platform. Interested suppliers are encouraged to register their interest to gain access to the tender documentation.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Queensland Rail<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 04/Sep/2026 04:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP518426<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Transport, Freight, Logistics<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=94cd92c9ae194f388e3d2f509b990351s518426s6d10084572b34143a0919a94482adc7es1606</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">94cd92c9ae194f388e3d2f509b990351</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:05:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Transport, Freight, Logistics</category>
</item>
<item><title>Rectification of the Wolgan Road Landslip</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Lithgow City Council is seeking proposals from suitable consultants to design and construct a solution to a roadside landslip on Wolgan Road, within the Wolgan Valley. The section of road affected is positioned adjacent to the Wolgan River. In 2022, following a heavy rain event, the river rose significantly and scoured the side of the bank away, leading to the landslip, affecting the roadway above.<br /><br />The site is located within the Wolgan Valley and access is currently restricted due to a larger landslip that has led to construction of a temporary access road known as the 'Donkey Steps'.<br /><br />A mandatory site inspection is scheduled for 10:30am, Tuesday 18th August. Further details regarding this inspection are included in Volume 1 of the tender documents.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Lithgow City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Sep/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519788<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Engineer, Research, Tech services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=bc78d08613694b618c14a0f6e6160892s519788</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">bc78d08613694b618c14a0f6e6160892</guid>
<pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 23:38:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
<category>Engineer, Research, Tech services</category>
</item>
<item><title>Design, Build and Implementation of the AFFIRMS Reporting System</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> AFAC is seeking a suitably qualified supplier to support the design and implementation of the Australasian Fire Fatality and Injury Reporting and Monitoring System (AFFIRMS). AFFIRMS is a national evidence and research utilisation initiative aimed at improving the consistency, quality and accessibility of fire fatality and injury data across Australia and New Zealand. The successful supplier will work with AFAC member agencies to review existing data sources and methodologies, develop a sustainable reporting framework, support data governance arrangements, and establish processes that enable meaningful analysis and reporting. While technology may form part of the solution, this is primarily a research, data and evidence-based project rather than a standalone software development procurement. Services may be delivered remotely, with project commencement anticipated in late 2026.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> AFAC<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 13/Sep/2026 10:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519678<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Community & Social Services, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Healthcare Services, Training & Development<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=f21490e606b3491dae2772633a5ad2c9s519678</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">f21490e606b3491dae2772633a5ad2c9</guid>
