</item>
<item><title>CTG Replacement</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Metro South Health (MSH) is undertaking a strategic procurement to replace ageing Cardiotocography (CTG) monitoring systems across its maternity services. CTG systems are critical clinical monitoring devices used during both antepartum and intrapartum care to monitor foetal heart rate and uterine activity, supporting the assessment of foetal wellbeing and enabling timely clinical intervention when required.<br /><br />MSH currently operates approximately 65 CTG monitoring systems across its facilities, of which 40 units have been nominated for replacement for this procurement.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Metro South Hospital and Health Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 31/Aug/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519532<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Alex Ovenden Email: alexander.ovenden@health.qld.gov.au Tel: 0735640318<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Medical Equipment. & Supplies<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 7]]></description>
