<item><title>PT01-26/27 Toowoomba Regional Art Gallery (TRAG) Remediation Project - Client Side Project Advisor</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Toowoomba Regional Art Gallery (TRAG) is a Council-owned heritage-listed facility and a key cultural asset within the Toowoomba Region. The gallery plays an important role in delivering cultural, artistic and community outcomes in alignment with Council’s strategic objectives.<br /><br />The building has experienced ongoing condition issues, including water ingress and environmental control failures, which have impacted its ability to safely accommodate the collection and support gallery operations. Following a significant weather event in November 2025, the gallery was closed and the collection relocated to off-site storage.<br /><br />Council has undertaken investigations into the condition of the building and commissioned a Front-End Engineering Design (FEED) Study to identify remediation options, associated risks and potential delivery pathways. The project will progress through a staged approach, including design development and construction, to restore the facility to an operational standard that me...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Aug/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519214<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=af19822af9954e5db3a404d4de98bf91s519214</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">af19822af9954e5db3a404d4de98bf91</guid>
