<item><title>Grand Promenade Reserve - Cricket Nets Replacement</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The City of Bayswater (“the Principal”) is a WA local government located approximately eight kilometres north-east of the Perth CBD. It includes the suburbs of Bayswater, Bedford, Embleton, Morley, Noranda, Maylands and parts of Mount Lawley and Dianella.<br /><br />The Principal is seeking quotations from suitably qualified and experienced contractors for the supply and installation of new cricket nets at Grand Promenade Reserve, located in Bedford WA 6052 (“the Works”). The Works will include supplying and installing a 4-bay cricket practice facility, removing dividing fencing, new concrete slabs, new synthetic turf and new rubber matting.<br /><br />The Statement of Requirement (Part 2 of this Request) sets out a full description of the Principal’s requirements in relation to this Request.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Bayswater<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 20/Aug/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+08:00) Perth time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP518756<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
