<item><title>WT01-26/27 Construction of Water Main and Associated Ancillaries in Glenvale</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council (TRC) is looking for a contractor to construct watermain upgrades to improve drinking water supply in and around the Glenvale area. The Glenvale Reservoir, located on Skyline Drive, provides water to Glenvale (west of Boundary Street), Westbrook, and Wyreema Reservoir. It is filled from the Kynoch Zone via a reticulation network.<br /><br />TRC has identified two main issues affecting this water supply:<br /><br />• Insufficient pressure to fill the Glenvale Reservoir at the required flow rate.<br /><br />• High water velocities along Riethmuller Road and parts of Boundary Street, which cause pressure drops in other areas, - especially near Hursley Road - reducing supply to Westbrook and Wyreema.<br /><br />To address these issues, TRC's 2023 Water Supply Planning Report: Greater Western Toowoomba Water Supply Study recommends several upgrades. The scope of this contract includes two of these recommended improvements, as outlined below:<br /><br />• Augmentation GLW_21_6: A new DN25...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 19/Aug/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP518005<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 15]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=ab905dcc452c4bbb8edd075fc5b9b512s518005s786e232eacbb4e31b23c50bf234a0226s1611</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">ab905dcc452c4bbb8edd075fc5b9b512</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 05:27:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Water &amp; Sewage</category>
</item>
<item><title>Advance Tender Notice - Road Infrastructure Investigation and Design PSA</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> ADVANCED TENDER NOTICE<br /><br />The City of Moreton Bay (Council) provides prospective tenderers with an advance notice of its intent to invite Tenders to establish a Preferred Supplier Arrangement (PSA) for Road Infrastructure Investigation and Design. Moreton Bay City Council requires these Services, to support the operational needs of the city.<br /><br />The PSA scope will include the following to the extent related to road infrastructure:<br /><br />Pavement investigation and design services<br /><br />Traffic/intersection volume survey<br /><br />Geotechnical testing<br /><br />Pavement testing <br /><br />Road safety audits<br /><br />RPEQ services <br /><br />The purpose of this Vendor Panel (VP) event is an Advertisement only. There is no need to provide a response to this VP event or register your interest. For clarity a Close Date and Expected Decision Date are only listed due to being mandatory VP fields.<br /><br /><br /><br />TENDER DETAILS<br /><br />Council anticipates the Tender opportunity...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Moreton Bay<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Aug/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP518003<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 0]]></description>
